<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dahir Riyale Kahin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1952">1952</a>–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dahir Riyale Kahin is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-somaliland">Somaliland</a> politician who was president of Somaliland from 2002 to 2010. Vice-president under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-haji-ibrahim-egal">Muhammad Haji Ibrahim Egal</a>, he succeeded him on his death in May 2002 and won the 2003 election by about 80 votes, a result the opposition accepted. He lost the 2010 election to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmed-mohamed-mohamoud">Ahmed Mohamed Mohamoud</a> (Silanyo) and handed over power peacefully.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dahir-riyale-kahin.jpg" alt="Dahir Riyale Kahin" width="302" height="396" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dahir_Riyaale_Kahin_(3x4_cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
